statement:
Put
\[
E=\frac{16072081}{640000000}.
\]
Let
\[
x,a,h,c,s,t,g,G,y>0,\qquad 0<h<12,\qquad 0<c<12-h,
\]
and define
\[
L=12-h,\qquad d=s+t,\qquad Y=\frac{Ld}{c}.
\]
Define the four coordinate cell areas
\[
\begin{aligned}
a_1&=\frac{xg}{2},\\
a_{13}&=12x+\frac{x^2}{2}+\frac{(12+x)a}{2},\\
a_{123}&=12h-\frac{h^2}{2}+\frac{Lc}{2},\\
a_{12}
&=\frac{h(g+G)}2
+\frac{(c+s)(G+y)}2
+\frac{t(y+Y)}2
-\frac{Ld^2}{2c}.
\end{aligned}
\]
Suppose that
\[
-\frac{12+x}{a}
\le 1-\frac gx
\le 1-\frac{G-g}{h}
\le 1-\frac{y-G}{c+s}
\le 1-\frac{Y-y}{t}
\tag{1}
\]
and
\[
\frac9{5000}E\le a_1\le\frac{11}{5000}E,\qquad
a_{13}\ge\frac{27}{10}E,\qquad
a_{123}\le\frac{11}{10}E.
\tag{2}
\]
Then
\[
a_{12}
<
\frac{8453526281}{99008000000}
<
\frac9{100}
\tag{3}
\]
and, for
\[
\Delta_{\rm kink}
=\frac{(c+d)y-tG-(c+s)Y}{2},
\]
\[
0\le\Delta_{\rm kink}<\frac{16}{595}
<\frac3{40}
<
\frac{
38147810777079388186060782356906840980757
}{
477534754162653027653180705158400000000000
}.
\tag{4}
\]
Consequently (1)--(2) are incompatible with the ten-percent-box
condition
\[
a_{12}\ge\frac{17991}{5000}E
=\frac9{100}
+\frac{1152809271}{3200000000000}.
\tag{5}
\]
In particular, neither the exact target nor any point in the full
ten-percent box can satisfy the nine-vertex system.
